{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-45736",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "ws is an open source WebSocket client and server for Node.js. Prior to ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "ws is an open source WebSocket client and server for Node.js. Prior to 8.20.1, the websocket.close() implementation is vulnerable to uninitialized memory disclosure when a TypedArray is passed as the reason argument. This vulnerability is fixed in 8.20.1."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45736",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-45736\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: ws\nFixed Version: 8.20.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-45736](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45736)\nws is an open source WebSocket client and server for Node.js. Prior to 8.20.1, the websocket.close() implementation is vulnerable to uninitialized memory disclosure when a TypedArray is passed as the reason argument. This vulnerability is fixed in 8.20.1.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-45736**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|ws|8.20.1|[CVE-2026-45736](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45736)|\n\nws is an open source WebSocket client and server for Node.js. Prior to 8.20.1, the websocket.close() implementation is vulnerable to uninitialized memory disclosure when a TypedArray is passed as the reason argument. This vulnerability is fixed in 8.20.1."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 4.4,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "4.4",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS-0002",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Image user should not be 'root'"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Running containers with 'root' user can lead to a container escape situation. It is a best practice to run containers as non-root users, which can be done by adding a 'USER' statement to the Dockerfile."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0002",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0002\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: HIGH\nCheck: Image user should not be 'root'\nMessage: Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user as argument\nLink: [DS-0002](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0002)\nRunning containers with 'root' user can lead to a container escape situation. It is a best practice to run containers as non-root users, which can be done by adding a 'USER' statement to the Dockerfile.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0002**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|HIGH|Image user should not be 'root'|Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user as argument|[DS-0002](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0002)|\n\nRunning containers with 'root' user can lead to a container escape situation. It is a best practice to run containers as non-root users, which can be done by adding a 'USER' statement to the Dockerfile."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "DS-0026",
              "name": "Misconfiguration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "No HEALTHCHECK defined"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "You should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026",
              "help": {
                "text": "Misconfiguration DS-0026\nType: Dockerfile Security Check\nSeverity: LOW\nCheck: No HEALTHCHECK defined\nMessage: Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile\nLink: [DS-0026](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026)\nYou should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers.",
                "markdown": "**Misconfiguration DS-0026**\n| Type | Severity | Check | Message | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|Dockerfile Security Check|LOW|No HEALTHCHECK defined|Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile|[DS-0026](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026)|\n\nYou should add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your docker container images to perform the health check on running containers."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "misconfiguration",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.71.0"
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CVE-2026-45736",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Package: ws\nInstalled Version: 8.20.0\nVulnerability CVE-2026-45736\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nFixed Version: 8.20.1\nLink: [CVE-2026-45736](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-45736)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "package-lock.json",
                  "uriBaseId": "ROOTPATH"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1318,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endLine": 1338,
                  "endColumn": 1
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "package-lock.json: ws@8.20.0"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "DS-0002",
          "ruleIndex": 1,
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Artifact: Dockerfile\nType: dockerfile\nVulnerability DS-0002\nSeverity: HIGH\nMessage: Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user as argument\nLink: [DS-0002](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0002)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "Dockerfile",
                  "uriBaseId": "ROOTPATH"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endLine": 1,
                  "endColumn": 1
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Dockerfile"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "DS-0026",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Artifact: Dockerfile\nType: dockerfile\nVulnerability DS-0026\nSeverity: LOW\nMessage: Add HEALTHCHECK instruction in your Dockerfile\nLink: [DS-0026](https://avd.aquasec.com/misconfig/ds-0026)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "Dockerfile",
                  "uriBaseId": "ROOTPATH"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 1,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endLine": 1,
                  "endColumn": 1
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Dockerfile"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "columnKind": "utf16CodeUnits",
      "originalUriBaseIds": {
        "ROOTPATH": {
          "uri": "file:///src/"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}